    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_17933">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_73558"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A hydroxycalciol that is calciol in which the hydrogen at position 25 has been replaced by a hydroxy group. A prehormone resulting from the oxidation of calciol in the liver, it is further hydroxylated in the kidney to give calcitriol, the active form of vitamin D&lt;small&gt;&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/small&gt;.</obo:IAO_0000115>
