        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_36615"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A ginsenoside found in &lt;em&gt;Panax ginseng&lt;/em&gt; that is dammarane which is substituted by hydroxy groups at the 3β, 12β and 20 &lt;em&gt;pro&lt;/em&gt;-&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt; positions, in which the hydroxy groups at positions 3 and 20 have been converted to the corresponding β-&lt;small&gt;D&lt;/small&gt;-glucopyranosyl-(1→2)-β-&lt;small&gt;D&lt;/small&gt;-glucopyranoside and α-&lt;small&gt;L&lt;/small&gt;-arabinofuranosyl-(1→6)-β-&lt;small&gt;D&lt;/small&gt;-glucopyranoside respectively, and in which a double bond has been introduced at the 24-25 position.</obo:IAO_0000115>
